The Project Raven aircraft are designed around the following engineering principles:

1. Reliability over maximum performance.
2. Stability in wind over top speed.
3. Modular design for future upgrades.
4. Repairability using commercially available components.
5. Comprehensive documentation of all engineering decisions.
6. Validation of new hardware and software on the Raven Mk I before integration into the Raven Mk II.
